0 // Essential-only hot press. A slider-crank, drive on top.
0 // The motor is pinned by two pegs to a purple Technic brick on a red
0 // tower. One peg in the motor's turning hub is the crank, radius 20 LDU.
0 // The blue 7M beam is the rod, 120 LDU hole to hole. It pulls a green
0 // plate that slides on two black axles. A red brick under the plate is
0 // the hot press head. At the bottom of the turn it stops 4 LDU (1.6 mm)
0 // over the tan wood's studs, so the motor never stalls on the wood.
0 // This file is the top of the turn: the press is open.

0 // Step 1 -- the table.
1 15 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 91405.dat
0 STEP
0 // Step 2 -- the bottom hot plate. Long side across, studs on the
0 // middle eight.
1 4 0 -24 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 39789.dat
0 STEP
0 // Step 3 -- the old wood, two tan plates. Studs reach y = -44.
1 191 0 -32 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3709.dat
1 191 0 -40 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3709.dat
0 STEP
0 // Step 4 -- the guide sockets. Cross holes on x = +-60, so the green
0 // plate's end holes line up with them.
1 288 -60 -24 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 6143.dat
1 288 60 -24 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 6143.dat
0 STEP
0 // Step 5 -- the guide axles. Low end at y = -8, top at -167.
1 0 -60 -87.5 0 0 1 0 -1 0 0 0 0 1 3707.dat
1 0 60 -87.5 0 0 1 0 -1 0 0 0 0 1 3707.dat
0 STEP
0 // Step 6 -- the press plate. Round end holes on the two axles, so it
0 // slides. Up pose: top at y = -120.
1 10 0 -120 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3738.dat
0 STEP
0 // Step 7 -- the press head, red, under the plate. Its studs go up into
0 // the plate. Bottom at -88 here and -48 at the bottom of the turn.
1 4 0 -112 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 39789.dat
0 STEP
0 // Step 8 -- the hinge. Red 1x2 with two holes, on the front row of the
0 // plate. The lower hole (10 over the plate) is the one the rod uses.
1 4 0 -128 10 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 32530.dat
0 STEP
0 // Step 9 -- the tower, three red 2x2x3 bricks behind the press. 216 tall.
1 4 0 -72 -80 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 30145.dat
1 4 0 -144 -80 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 30145.dat
1 4 0 -216 -80 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 30145.dat
0 STEP
0 // Step 10 -- the motor mount. Purple Technic 1x4 on the tower's front
0 // row, holes at hub height (y = -230) and pointing front to back.
0 // Orange 1x4 on the back row.
1 26 0 -240 -70 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3701.dat
1 25 0 -240 -90 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3010.dat
0 STEP
0 // Step 11 -- the cap. A red 2x4 tile locks the two 1x4s together.
1 4 0 -248 -80 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 87079.dat
0 STEP
0 // Step 12 -- two pegs in the purple brick's outer holes, out the front.
1 0 -20 -230 -60 0 0 -1 0 1 0 1 0 0 61332.dat
1 0 20 -230 -60 0 0 -1 0 1 0 1 0 0 61332.dat
0 STEP
0 // Step 13 -- the motor, hub to the front. Its two back holes at hub
0 // height take the two pegs. Back face on z = -60, hub face on z = 20.
1 15 0 -230 -30 -1 0 0 0 0 -1 0 -1 0 68488.dat
0 STEP
0 // Step 14 -- two pegs: one in the hub's top hole (the crank), one in
0 // the hinge's lower hole.
1 0 0 -250 20 0 0 -1 0 1 0 1 0 0 61332.dat
1 0 0 -130 20 0 0 -1 0 1 0 1 0 0 61332.dat
0 STEP
0 // Step 15 -- the rod. Blue 7M beam on both pegs: top hole on the crank,
0 // bottom hole on the hinge.
1 1 0 -190 30 1 0 0 0 0 -1 0 1 0 32524.dat
0 STEP
0 // Step 16 -- the face. Two pegs in the motor's front holes, 60 over
0 // the hub, and a big eye tile on each peg end.
1 0 -20 -290 0 0 0 -1 0 1 0 1 0 0 61332.dat
1 0 20 -290 0 0 0 -1 0 1 0 1 0 0 61332.dat
1 15 -20 -290 24 1 0 0 0 0 1 0 -1 0 14769.dat
1 15 20 -290 24 1 0 0 0 0 1 0 -1 0 14769.dat
0 STEP
0 // Step 17 -- two lights on top: a peg in each top hole, a red crystal
0 // and a green crystal on the peg ends.
1 0 -20 -300 -30 0 1 0 -1 0 0 0 0 1 61332.dat
1 0 20 -300 -30 0 1 0 -1 0 0 0 0 1 61332.dat
1 36 -20 -336 -30 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 11127.dat
1 35 20 -336 -30 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 11127.dat
0 STEP
0 // Step 18 -- super wood: one tan plate, half as thick, in front.
1 191 -100 -8 80 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3709.dat
0 STEP
